stion/id #uuid "dd7403df-a496-59c6-8226-c07a3e6dd8d2" :question/math-academy-id "q-158123" :question/problem "Find the vector in the subspace spanned by ${{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}$ \nthat is closest to the vector $x,$ where \n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -6 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that ${a}_{1}$ and ${a}_{2}$ are linearly independent. \n\nThe closest vector to $x$ in the subspace spanned by ${{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}$ is orthogonal projection of $x$ onto the subspace, which is given by\n\n$$\n{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x=A({A}^{T}\\,A)^{-1}\\,{A}^{T}\\,x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}| & | \\\\ {a}_{1} & {a}_{2} \\\\ | & |\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\,⟹\\,{A}^{T}=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get the following projection:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot {([\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}])}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -6 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot {[\\begin{aligned}10 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot \\frac{1}{26}[\\begin{aligned}3 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 10\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134243 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133789 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c07721dd-4b97-5d57-8de1-5098117e3071" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Orthogonal Projection of a Vector Onto a Plane"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a0deec70-86e2-5561-94e9-49625a85f72c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131498} {:answer/id #uuid "f7646e96-1638-5c5e-a52c-ef31107fbd80" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131499} {:answer/id #uuid "f90c3a1a-bf33-5e4f-a011-dff97cc5750b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131500} {:answer/id #uuid "1881ff21-b8dc-5252-90d7-7885b0d6e1b4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131501} {:answer/id #uuid "20cb1a68-2cdc-530d-b2d1-eb3f08800123" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131502}] :answer-field/id #uuid "878a4e45-5d30-5f1c-aefb-67035a88d122" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131497}] :question/id #uuid "c6ef098f-928d-59a3-9d4f-bfcb112bab97" :question/math-academy-id "q-39869" :question/problem "Find the orthogonal projection of the vector $x$ onto the plane $r = sv + tw$, where $s, t ∈ R$, and\n$v = \\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}, w = \\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}, x = \\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}$.\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question." :question/requires-calculator true}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186394738 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133789 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c07721dd-4b97-5d57-8de1-5098117e3071" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Orthogonal Projection of a Vector Onto a Plane"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4de82d8c-ce23-555b-bc98-20cd4b7e3d00" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394740} {:answer/id #uuid "9d838a17-fcf6-5cd8-b98f-01a452dd4e52" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394741} {:answer/id #uuid "931f8ee6-6ee9-5feb-989f-f94e1f389d53" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394742} {:answer/id #uuid "134407e9-0936-586f-9d57-4a275793781d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394743} {:answer/id #uuid "5fb70189-b1c1-5b51-aee9-863f62dd9e9a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394744}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5fb70189-b1c1-5b51-aee9-863f62dd9e9a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394744} :answer-field/id #uuid "a2d2041b-3a0c-511a-ae57-4e83abdb08e1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394739}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "734db729-9741-5fdd-a351-d012beb5fb6b" :question/math-academy-id "q-86761" :question/problem "Find the orthogonal projection of the vector $x$ onto the plane $r=sv+tw,$ where $s,t\\in R,$ and\n\n$$\nv=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],\\,w=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -8\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that $v$ and $w$ are linearly independent. \n\nThe orthogonal projection of $x$ onto the subspace $S$ spanned by the columns of a matrix $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x=A({A}^{T}\\,A)^{-1}\\,{A}^{T}\\,x.\n$$\n\nSince our plane passes through the origin, it defines the subspace $S=\\text{Span}{v,w}$ in ${R}^{3}.$ In our case, we have\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}| & | \\\\ v & w \\\\ | & |\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & \\,\\,-2 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\,⟹\\,{A}^{T}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 2 & -2 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get the following projection:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & \\,\\,-2 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot {([\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 2 & -2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & \\,\\,-2 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}])}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 2 & -2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -8\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & \\,\\,-2 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot {[\\begin{aligned}11 & -5 \\\\ -5 & 9\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & \\,\\,-2 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot \\frac{1}{74}[\\begin{aligned}9 & 5 \\\\ 5 & 11\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & \\,\\,-2 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
